  :adr/body "# ADR-2607251552: toshokan-patents — worldwide patent bibliographic resident harvest\n\n**Status**: draft (pending live USPTO verification)\n**Date**: 2026-07-25\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed under standing authorization)\n\n## Context\n\nOwner request: design + implement worldwide patent acquisition, store as EDN, query via Datomic/DataScript, resident on murakumo.cloud.\n\nInvestigation found the workspace already has **two running self-growing resident harvesters** of exactly the shape this needs:\n- `kotoba-lang/toshokan` (ADR-2607199900 + 2607255100): national library bibliographic metadata. `daemon.cljs` + `seeds.edn` + `80-data/public/*.journal.edn` (quads) + kotobase fold + LaunchAgent `com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-tick` (6h).\n- `com-junkawasaki/product-corpus` (ADR-2607252100): web-wide product corpus via Common Crawl. Same daemon/state/targets/DataLad shape, verified with real data (545 WARC → 372 Product).\n\nmurakumo also already has a **measured fleet task plane** (ADR-2607256000: 11 nodes, 132 cores, 22 tasks @ 10.01x speedup, accepted) and a **sandboxed agent loop PoC** (ADR-2607252600, accepted) whose follow-up #4 is the standing-tick — the one missing piece for residency.\n\nSo this is **not** a greenfield actor-host / cloud-murakumo-Cron / GitHub-App build. It is a toshokan-pattern replication for the patent domain. An earlier draft design (cloud-murakumo Cron Trigger + GitHub App + commit `1cd0aa2`) was based on a stale 150-behind local checkout that missed these landed assets; it is withdrawn by this ADR.\n\n## Decision\n\nCreate `kotoba-lang/toshokan-patents` as a sibling of `toshokan`, replicating the ADR-2607255100 self-growing resident harvest pattern:\n\n1. **Scope: metadata-only patent bibliographic** — title, applicant, inventor, number, kind, filed/granted dates, IPC/CPC classification, status, applicant-LEI (join key). Claims full text is a separate B2/DataLad plane if ever added; it is NOT carried in git journals (history explosion, same call as toshokan full-text).\n2. **Sources, added incrementally with live verification** (same discipline as toshokan's one-jurisdiction-at-a-time):\n   - **USPTO first** — Open Data Portal / PatentsView (CC BY 4.0, JSON, public domain under 17 USC §105). Lowest friction, proves the loop end-to-end.\n   - **JPO** — Standardized Data TSV (no auth, daily/weekly, F-term classification).\n   - **EPO DOCDB** — BDDS public area (no auth since 2025-02, ST.36 XML, ~150M records, 100+ offices). The eventual \"worldwide\" master; brought in once ST.36 parsing is proven on USPTO+JPO. Heavy backfill fans out via `murakumo task run` (ADR-2607256000).\n   - **WIPO PATENTSCOPE** — bulk explicitly prohibited → `:spec` only, same treatment as toshokan's iran-nlai / russia-rsl (calling `search` throws, not a silent no-op).\n3. **Schema**: `:patent/*` attributes; entity ids namespaced by office (`uspto:<patent-number>`, `jpo:<app-number>`, `epo:<pub-number>`). Quads `[entity attr value tx op]` in `80-data/public/<office>.journal.edn`, the git-authoritative shape from ADR-2607072300.\n4. **Residency**: macOS LaunchAgent `com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-patents-tick` (StartInterval 21600 = 6h) running `daemon.cljs --once --push --ingest`. Same class as `toshokan-tick` / `fleet-ci-murakumo-tick` / `itonami-qwen36-tick`. This is the honest production path today and lands task-plane follow-up #4 (\"常設 tick 化\") for the patent domain.\n5. **Query**: a patent loader is added to `manifest/edn-query.cljs` (same shape as the J-category / toshokan loaders), with `:source/dataset \"patent\"`, joining `:patent/applicant-lei` → `:company/lei` so financials × legal-entity × patents resolve in one query on the ADR-2607252000 plane.\n6. **Fleet fan-out (later, not v1)**: the heavy DOCDB worldwide backfill uses `murakumo task run` (ADR-2607256000). Not needed for the USPTO-first proving slice.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) Answers the owner request with a **real running loop**, not a paper design — and reuses a verified, in-production pattern with no new actor host, no cloud-murakumo Cron, no GitHub App.\n\n(+) Worldwide coverage is **asymptotic and honest**: USPTO proves the loop with live data, then JPO, then EPO DOCDB brings ~85–90% of world patenting by volume. No fabricated \"complete global inventory\" claim on day one (CLAUDE.md system-dynamics rule: a model that can accept any entity, computed honestly on the data we have).\n\n(-) **LaunchAgent on the fleet host** that has git credentials and network, not a WASM `on-tick` guest on murakumo. Upgrade to the ADR-2607252400 CID-capability guest path is non-exclusive and waits on that capability landing.\n\n(-) **metadata-only**: no claims full text in the queryable graph. If claims text is wanted later, it goes to a B2/DataLad annex plane (skill `large-binary-datalad`), not into journal quads.\n\n(-) **EPO DOCDB licence** (Art 5.4): raw data may not be redistributed. The corpus stays a private research corpus behind owner auth; any UI built on it carries the Art 10.2 attribution. Storage in a private corpus is within Art 5.2 internal-use.\n\n## Alternatives rejected\n\n| option | why not |\n|---|---|\n| cloud-murakumo Cron Trigger + GitHub App + commit `1cd0aa2` (earlier draft) | based on a stale 150-behind local that missed landed task plane + LaunchAgent residency; GitHub App is unnecessary for a git-push-from-Mac tick; withdrawn |\n| greenfield wasmcloud-like actor host on murakumo | wasmCloud cannot run on Cloudflare Workers (V8 isolate ≠ Wasmtime host); Cloudflare native (Cron + DO + Queue + `cloudflare/actors`) already covers the model; overkill for one weekly job |\n| per-patent repos (LEI `cloud-itonami-lei-*` pattern) | patents are 150M+ records; one-repo-per-record does not scale. market-intel flat-vector or toshokan journal-per-source is correct |\n| Google Patents BigQuery as primary | GitHub repo archived 2026-04-18; freshness uncertain. Usable as a one-time normalized bootstrap only if ST.36 parsing proves prohibitive |\n| full-text claims in git journals | history explosion; use B2/DataLad annex if ever added (skill `large-binary-datalad`) |\n\n## Implementation pointers\n\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan-patents/scripts/daemon.cljs` (copied from toshokan, `sources` map swapped to patent offices)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan-patents/src/toshokan_patents/sources/uspto.cljs` (new — USPTO ODP/PatentsView API client)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/toshokan-patents/deploy/com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-patents-tick.plist`\n- `manifest/edn-query.cljs` patent loader (added in the implementation step)\n\n## Verification (2026-07-25 session close — implemented & resident)\n\nv1 is live, not paper. End-to-end measured:\n\n- **Source pivot**: USPTO ODP API was mid-migration (search.patentsview.org sunset 2026-03; data.uspto.gov path fluid). v1 ships with **Google Patents individual pages** instead — public, no-auth, worldwide (US/EP/JP/WO/CN/KR...), rich Dublin Core / citation_* metadata, and the page carries DC.relation references so the daemon self-grows by walking the **citation graph** (patent-domain analogue of toshokan growing seeds from creators).\n- **Self-growth**: 4 root seeds → **144 patents / 790+ citation edges** (the parallel community-coverage session advanced it; the citation graph keeps expanding every tick).\n- **EDN store**: `[entity attr value tx op]` quads in `80-data/public/google-patents.journal.edn`, git-authoritative (ADR-2607072300).\n- **Unified query plane (ADR-2607252000)**: patent loader in `manifest/edn-query.cljs` (PR #1277). **gap 2 join** — `normalize-name` + `:patent/applicant-norm` + `:company/legal-name-norm` lets patent assignees resolve to LEI: verified **BASF SE** patents → **LEI 529900PM64WH8AF1E917** on the 95,459-entity plane (PR #1288).\n- **kotobase fold (gap 1)**: `scripts/kotobase-ingest-toshokan-patents.cljs` folds journals into the `kotobase.net` graph `toshokan-patents` (self-minted did:key).\n- **Residency**: LaunchAgent `com.kotoba-lang.toshokan-patents-tick` (6h, `daemon.cljs --once --push --ingest`); self-growing git push per tick.\n- **tamaki registration**: the tick is wrapped as `tamaki exec` → an `:agent.run/mode :external` AgentRun in `~/.tamaki/events.edn`; `tamaki status` shows every tick alongside model-driven agent runs with its real exit code (mirrors innen-tick; the deterministic tick is not falsely recorded as a kotoba-code run).\n\nPRs: #1275 (manifest register), #1277 (query-plane loader + this ADR), #1288 (gap 2 join + ADR parse fixes).\n\nFollow-ups (out of v1 scope, not blocking): EPO DOCDB worldwide backfill via `murakumo task run` (ADR-2607256000); JPO standardized-data TSV source; USPTO ODP API once it stabilises; claims full text on a B2/DataLad annex plane; resolve the behind-2 force-push on kotoba-fleet/murakumo (separate owner/community-coverage matter).\n"}]
